# ORCLPASS: passage teleport, post-passage unpause, board-edge transfer (M16.3
# and M16.7's return trip). Board 0 "Pass Hub": player 30,13, cyan passage
# 32,13 -> "Pass Target". "Pass Target": arrival passage 34,13, border gap
# 60,14, east exit -> "Pass East" (entry gap 1,14). The arrival leaves the
# player paused ON the passage tile; the next move must unpause via the stamp
# branch, leaving the passage tile intact (the M16.2 finding this sweep
# covers and fixes). M16.7 appends a return crossing: "Pass East"'s west exit
# points back to "Pass Target" through the same gap row, so leaving via the
# east edge and immediately crossing back west proves board re-entry lands at
# the crossing edge's mirrored coordinate (ElementBoardEdgeTouch,
# elements.go), not the board's own start-player square — vanilla only uses
# StartPlayerX/Y for the very first title->play spawn or a zap re-enter.
world ORCLPASS
seed 0
boot 240
capture title
play
move right
# touch the passage: teleport to Pass Target, arrive paused on the passage
move right
capture arrival
# unpause off a non-player tile: player steps south, passage stays visible
move down
capture unpaused
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
# stand on the border gap at 60,14 and cross the eastern board edge
capture atedge
move right
capture east
# re-enter "Pass Target" through the same gap, from the opposite side
move left
capture backatpasstarget
